   "text": {
    "L1": "An island is land with water all around it. It is the top of land rising from the sea floor.",
    "L2": "An island does not float like a boat. It stays connected to land below the sea.",
    "L3": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands have thick rainforests, mangroves and coral reefs.",
    "L4": "Coral reefs are built by tiny coral animals called polyps. They shelter a huge variety of sea life.",
    "L5": "The Western Ghats are a long chain of hills along India's west coast.",
    "L6": "Moist monsoon winds from the Arabian Sea rise over the hills and drop heavy rain on the sea-facing side.",
    "L7": "The far side gets much less rain. Warmth and heavy rain help thick forests grow there.",
    "L8": "Now show what you know: which side of the Western Ghats gets more rain?"
   },
